<body><div class="urus-mobile-nav" style="display:none;position:sticky;top:0;z-index:1000;background:#0b0b0b;color:#c9a24d;padding:10px 16px;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.7px;border-bottom:1px solid #222">URUS · Agricultural Funding Intelligence</div>
<div class="page">
<!-- ══ PORTADA ══════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="cover">
<div class="cover-urus">URUS</div>
<div class="cover-sub">Agricultural Intelligence</div>
<div class="cover-divider"></div>
<div class="cover-title">Complete Federal Funding Report for Farms and Agricultural Projects in Puerto Rico</div>
<div class="cover-meta">
<strong>Date:</strong> August 8, 2026<br/>
<strong>Programs identified:</strong> 16 active or upcoming federal funding programs<br/>
<strong>Agencies monitored:</strong> USDA FSA · NRCS Caribbean · USDA Rural Development · DOE · HUD/PRDOH · FEMA · EPA · JSF<br/>
<strong>Estimated potential:</strong> $50,000 – $1,000,000+ depending on operation type<br/>
<strong>Classification:</strong> Confidential · Client use only
  </div>
<div class="cover-intel">
<div class="cover-intel-label">Operational Intelligence Note</div>
<div class="cover-intel-text">The system detected that <strong>two funding windows expired this week</strong> — ASCF on August 7 and preliminary SDRP Stage on August 12 — without being captured. These programs represented significant direct payments for agricultural producers in Puerto Rico. <strong>The system identified what was left on the table and what is still available.</strong></div>
</div>
<div class="cover-still">
<div class="cover-still-text"><strong>What is still open:</strong> 14 programs with active windows — SDRP through August 12, EQIP and conservation year-round, REAP solar, VAPG value-added, CDBG-DR, HMGP, CRP, and NRCS Caribbean green funding. The complete analysis is on the following pages.</div>
</div>
<div class="cover-footer">URUS ∴ urusverify.com · August 2026</div>
</div>
<!-- ══ RESUMEN EJECUTIVO ════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="section">
<div class="section-label">Section 1</div>
<div class="section-title">Executive Summary</div>
<p style="font-size:15px;line-height:1.8;color:#374151;margin:20px 0">The URUS system monitored all relevant federal databases for agricultural producers in Puerto Rico and identified <strong>16 active or upcoming programs</strong> with potential from $50,000 to $1,000,000+ depending on crop type, farm size, and historical loss profile. This analysis was generated using public data — without requiring operation-specific information.</p>
<div class="metrics">
<div class="metric"><div class="metric-label">Programs Detected</div><div class="metric-value">16</div><div class="metric-sub">All agricultural sectors in PR</div></div>
<div class="metric"><div class="metric-label">Critical Urgency</div><div class="metric-value">2</div><div class="metric-sub">SDRP: 12 ago · ARC/PLC: 31 ago</div></div>
<div class="metric"><div class="metric-label">Maximum Potential</div><div class="metric-value">$1M+</div><div class="metric-sub">REAP + EQIP + VAPG combined</div></div>
<div class="metric"><div class="metric-label">Agencies</div><div class="metric-value">6</div><div class="metric-sub">FSA · NRCS · USDA RD · DOE · EPA · JSF</div></div>
<div class="metric"><div class="metric-label">Sectors</div><div class="metric-value">6</div><div class="metric-sub">Disaster · Green · Solar · Market · Insurance · Other</div></div>
</div>
<div class="urgency-block">
<div class="urgency-label">The Situation This Week</div>
<div class="urgency-text">
      ASCF (Specialty Crops) expired on August 7. SDRP expires on August 12. These two programs alone represent access to <strong>millions in direct federal assistance</strong> for producers with disaster losses in 2023-2024 and for fruit, coffee, vegetable, and specialty crop producers with acres reported in 2025.<br/><br/>
<strong>What remains:</strong> SDRP may still be active if the FSA administrative system has not been closed. There are 14 additional programs with open windows. The detailed analysis follows in the sections below — ordered by urgency.
    </div>
</div>
<div class="box-dark">
<div class="box-dark-label">What URUS Needs to Go to the Next Level</div>
<div class="box-dark-text">This analysis covers the full universe without operation-specific data. With the <strong>crop type, acreage, disaster loss history, and legal structure of the operation</strong>, the system can filter to the 3-5 programs with the highest probability of approval, calculate the estimated potential specific to this farm, and prepare the fastest path to the first funding opportunity.</div>
</div>
</div>
<!-- ══ URGENTS ═════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="section">
<div class="section-label">Section 2</div>
<div class="section-title">⚠ Urgent Deadlines — Immediate Action</div>
<!-- SDRP -->
<div class="grant-card" style="border-left:5px solid #dc2626">
<div class="grant-top" style="background:#fff8f8">
<div class="grant-top-left">
<h3>SDRP — Supplemental Disaster Relief Program</h3>
<div class="grant-top-agency">USDA Farm Service Agency (FSA) · American Relief Act 2025</div>
</div>
<div class="grant-top-right">
<span class="badge badge-red badge-block">⚠ URGENT</span>
<span class="badge badge-red badge-block">AUGUST 12, 2026</span>
</div>
</div>
<div class="grant-body">
<div class="grant-amount">$$16 billion available · Payments increased to 70% factor</div>
<div class="grant-deadline" style="color:#dc2626">Deadline: August 12, 2026</div>
<div class="grant-desc">Direct payments for losses to crops, trees, bushes, and vines from natural disasters in 2023 and 2024. Puerto Rico qualifies for Tropical Storm Ernesto (August 2024), Hurricane Fiona (2022), and prior events. USDA has already paid $6.7 billion and increased the factor to 70% — double the amount originally estimated. Covers insured losses (Stage 1) and uninsured losses including shallow losses (Stage 2).</div>
<div class="grant-detail"><strong>Stage 1:</strong> Losses covered by federal crop insurance or NAP. Applies with insurance documentation.</div>
<div class="grant-detail"><strong>Stage 2:</strong> Uninsured losses, shallow losses, and quality losses. Applies with damage documentation.</div>
<div class="grant-detail"><strong>PR qualifies for:</strong> Tropical Storm Ernesto (August 2024) · Hurricane Fiona (September 2022) · Seismic period (2020).</div>
<div class="grant-action">
<div class="grant-action-label">Required Action — Contact FSA Today</div>
<div class="grant-action-text">Contact FSA Puerto Rico immediately. Request an application for Stage 1 and/or Stage 2 according to the type of losses. Bring disaster loss documentation. Deadline: August 12.</div>
</div>
<div class="grant-contact">FSA Puerto Rico · (787) 294-1650 · fsa.usda.gov/sdrp</div>
</div>
</div>
<!-- ARC/PLC -->
<div class="grant-card" style="border-left:5px solid #d97706">
<div class="grant-top" style="background:#fffef8">
<div class="grant-top-left">
<h3>ARC/PLC — Base Acres Review (first time since 2002)</h3>
<div class="grant-top-agency">USDA Farm Service Agency · Working Families Tax Cuts Act</div>
</div>
<div class="grant-top-right">
<span class="badge badge-orange badge-block">⚠ URGENT</span>
<span class="badge badge-orange badge-block">31 AUGUST 2026</span>
</div>
</div>
<div class="grant-body">
<div class="grant-amount">First opportunity in 24 years to increase base acres · Impact on future payments</div>
<div class="grant-deadline" style="color:#d97706">Deadline: August 31, 2026 — 23 days</div>
<div class="grant-desc">ARC and PLC programs protect producers when market prices or revenues decline. The Working Families Tax Cuts Act allows base acres to be updated for the first time since 2002. Up to 30 million new eligible acres nationwide. Base acres determine the amount of future safety-net payments. Zero cost, zero risk — only a review with FSA.</div>
<div class="grant-detail"><strong>Elegibilidad:</strong> Owners of agricultural land with base acres registered with FSA Puerto Rico.</div>
<div class="grant-action">
<div class="grant-action-label">Required Action — Review Before August 31</div>
<div class="grant-action-text">Contact FSA Puerto Rico to review current base acres. No new application required. Quick process. May significantly increase future ARC/PLC payments.</div>
</div>
<div class="grant-contact">FSA Puerto Rico · fsa.usda.gov/state-offices/puerto-rico</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<!-- ══ CONSERVATION Y VERDE ═════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="section">
<div class="section-label">Section 3</div>
<div class="section-title">🌱 Conservation, Green Funding and Sustainability</div>
<p style="font-size:13px;color:#6b7280;margin:14px 0 24px">Programs administered by NRCS Caribbean Area — applications accepted year-round. These are among the most accessible and operationally impactful funding programs for farms in PR.</p>
<!-- EQIP -->
<div class="grant-card" style="border-left:5px solid #16a34a">
<div class="grant-top">
<div class="grant-top-left">
<h3>EQIP — Environmental Quality Incentives Program</h3>
<div class="grant-top-agency">USDA NRCS Caribbean Area · Puerto Rico y USVI</div>
</div>
<div class="grant-top-right">
<span class="badge badge-green badge-block">CONSERVATION</span>
<span class="badge badge-green badge-block">OPEN YEAR-ROUND</span>
</div>
</div>
<div class="grant-body">
<div class="grant-amount">Up to $450,000 per producer · Direct payments for implemented practices</div>
<div class="grant-deadline" style="color:#16a34a">Applications accepted year-round · 2026 cycle active</div>
<div class="grant-desc">NRCS Caribbean’s most comprehensive program. Funds the implementation of conservation practices with direct payments to producers. NRCS Caribbean has funded projects in PR involving regenerative agriculture ($100K), coffee agroforestry ($75K), and soil conservation systems on sloped land for more than 20 years.</div>
<div class="grant-detail"><strong>Eligible practices in PR:</strong> Efficient irrigation systems · Anti-erosion terraces · Ground cover · Coffee and cacao agroforestry · Silvopasture systems · Nutrient management · Sediment barriers.</div>
<div class="grant-detail"><strong>Elegibilidad:</strong> Agricultural producers with eligible land. Priority for socially disadvantaged producers, veterans, and small and medium-sized farms.</div>
<div class="grant-action">
<div class="grant-action-label">Required Action</div>
<div class="grant-action-text">Contact NRCS Caribbean Area in Guaynabo. Request an eligibility evaluation and list of available practices with payment rates. No fixed deadline.</div>
</div>
<div class="grant-contact">NRCS Caribbean Area · (787) 277-9764 · nrcs.usda.gov/state-offices/caribbean-area</div>
</div>
</div>
<!-- CSP -->
<div class="grant-card" style="border-left:5px solid #16a34a">
<div class="grant-top">
<div class="grant-top-left">
<h3>CSP — Conservation Stewardship Program</h3>
<div class="grant-top-agency">USDA NRCS Caribbean Area</div>
</div>
<div class="grant-top-right">
<span class="badge badge-green badge-block">CONSERVATION</span>
<span class="badge badge-green badge-block">OPEN</span>
</div>
</div>
<div class="grant-body">
<div class="grant-amount">Annual payments based on the level of conservation implemented and improved</div>
<div class="grant-deadline" style="color:#16a34a">Applications accepted year-round</div>
<div class="grant-desc">Rewards producers who already have good conservation practices and want to improve them. Annual payments for the duration of the contract. Complements EQIP — ideal for farms with existing practices that want to move to the next level.</div>
<div class="grant-detail"><strong>Elegibilidad:</strong> Producers with land under active production and basic conservation practices already implemented.</div>
<div class="grant-action">
<div class="grant-action-label">Required Action</div>
<div class="grant-action-text">Contact NRCS Caribbean Area. Apply alongside EQIP to maximize benefits. Evaluate current farm practices.</div>
</div>
<div class="grant-contact">NRCS Caribbean Area · nrcs.usda.gov/state-offices/caribbean-area</div>
</div>
</div>
<!-- ACEP -->
<div class="grant-card" style="border-left:5px solid #16a34a">
<div class="grant-top">
<div class="grant-top-left">
<h3>ACEP — Agricultural Conservation Easement Program</h3>
<div class="grant-top-agency">USDA NRCS Caribbean Area</div>
</div>
<div class="grant-top-right">
<span class="badge badge-green badge-block">LAND</span>
<span class="badge badge-green badge-block">ONGOING</span>
</div>
</div>
<div class="grant-body">
<div class="grant-amount">Payment of market value for land conservation rights</div>
<div class="grant-deadline" style="color:#16a34a">Ongoing applications — case-by-case evaluation</div>
<div class="grant-desc">NRCS pays agricultural landowners to establish permanent or long-term conservation easements. The owner retains possession. Ideal for land with fragile ecosystems, wetlands, forested areas, or high historical agricultural value.</div>
<div class="grant-action">
<div class="grant-action-label">Required Action</div>
